WEBVTT

NOTE tts=synthetic

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.900
When should a breaker tool be replaced?

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:09.100
A tool gets shorter as it works; at the shortest usable length in the manual it should be replaced.

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:15.267
The rear face the piston strikes can deform and spread over its edges; the spread edge jams in the bushing.

4
00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:20.733
A cracked tool can break at any time; check the bushings before fitting a new tool.

5
00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:28.367
Check the bushings and the retainer key as well; grease the key slot and the bushing surface when fitting.
